2. WHAT YOU MAY DO
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Author grants you a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable licence to:

  a) install and use the Software on any computer you own or control, for as many
     installations as you personally use;

  b) make backup copies for your own use;

  c) publish screenshots, video recordings, livestreams, reviews and tutorials
     showing the Software in use, including on commercial platforms and including
     for your own profit, without asking the Author.

     This is stated explicitly so nobody has to wonder. The only limit is that
     such material must not itself distribute the Software or any part of it —
     showing it is free, handing it out is not.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. YOUR OWN PROFILES AND TUNING FILES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Aircraft profiles (`profiles/*.profile`) and tuning files (`basis/*.cfg`) are
plain text. A profile you write yourself — the dataref bindings you verified and
the constants you measured on your own helicopter — is your work, not the
Author's.

You may use, modify, publish and sell such files freely. This agreement places no
restriction on them whatsoever, and the fact that a file was written for the
Software, follows its format or names it does not make it part of the Software.

This applies to files you have authored. It does not extend to the profiles and
tuning files supplied with the Software, which are covered by section 4.

